# WatchBird TODO
# Prioritized implementation plan - reliability first, then speed, platform-specific deferred

## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## PHASE 1: RECOGNITION RELIABILITY (High Priority)
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## These directly improve accuracy and reduce false positives/negatives.

### Low-Light & Quality Enhancement
- [ ] CLAHE preprocessing: Add adaptive histogram equalization before embedding
      → In face_embedder.py extract(), apply cv2.createCLAHE(clipLimit=2.0, tileGridSize=(8,8))
      → Config option: preprocessing.clahe_enabled (default: true)
      → ~1ms overhead, significant gain in low-light

- [ ] Motion blur detection: Compute Laplacian variance, skip frames below threshold
      → In quality.py, add blur_metric check: if laplacian_var < blur_threshold * 0.3, reject
      → Already partially implemented, needs hard cutoff integration

- [ ] Backlight detection: Check histogram bimodality (bright background + dark subject)
      → Skip frame if >60% pixels in top 10% brightness AND face region <30% brightness
      → Prevents silhouette false negatives

### Pose-Aware Matching
- [ ] Head pose penalty: Weight embeddings by estimated yaw/pitch from landmarks
      → Compute yaw from eye-to-eye vs nose offset ratio (SCRFD landmarks available)
      → Penalize quality score: quality *= max(0.3, 1.0 - abs(yaw)/90)
      → Reject if |yaw| > 60° or |pitch| > 45°

- [ ] Pose diversity check at enrollment: Warn if all samples are frontal (<15° yaw)
      → In enroll.py, compute pose variance across samples per identity
      → Log warning if std(yaw) < 10°, suggest more varied photos

### Unknown Rejection
- [ ] Explicit LLR unknown threshold: Add hard cutoff for "definitely unknown"
      → In unified_scorer.py score(): if best_llr < -0.5, force person_id=None
      → Prevents weak matches from being accepted as known
      → Config: thresholds.llr_unknown_cutoff (default: -0.5)


## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## PHASE 2: IFF & STATE STABILITY (High Priority)
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## Reduces identity flipping and premature state transitions.

### Identity Stability
- [ ] Consecutive identity bonus: Boost confidence for N consecutive same-identity frames
      → In TemporalAggregator, track streak_count for same person_id
      → Apply bonus: effective_score = score * (1 + 0.05 * min(streak_count, 10))
      → Rewards stable recognition, penalizes flipping

- [ ] Identity switch hysteresis: Require higher margin to switch to different person
      → Already have identity_switch_margin=0.05, increase to 0.10 for FRIENDLY+ states
      → Once locked, switching requires: new_score > old_score + 0.15

### CONFIRMED State Lock-In
- [ ] Demotion hysteresis: Require N consecutive low-confidence frames before demotion
      → In state_machine.py, add demotion_frame_count threshold (default: 10)
      → CONFIRMED → FRIENDLY only if: low_confidence_streak >= demotion_threshold
      → Prevents single-frame glitches from breaking confirmed state

- [ ] Embedding freeze for CONFIRMED: Stop updating centroid to prevent drift
      → In embedding_aggregator.py, add frozen flag checked before add_embedding()
      → Set frozen=True when track enters CONFIRMED, unfrozen on demotion
      → Prevents gradual centroid corruption from bad samples

- [ ] Re-verification interval: Periodic lightweight check for CONFIRMED tracks
      → Every 30s, force one embedding extraction and score check
      → If score drops below t_accept - 0.1, unflag frozen and demote to FRIENDLY
      → Catches costume changes, impostor takeover

### Occlusion Handling
- [ ] Landmark spread ratio: Detect partial faces via landmark geometry
      → Compute: spread = dist(left_eye, right_mouth) / expected_spread
      → If spread < 0.6, flag as occluded, apply 0.7x confidence penalty
      → Uses existing SCRFD landmarks, no additional model needed

### Armed State Persistence
- [ ] Sticky "armed" classification: Once detected armed, require higher threshold to clear
      → In run_runtime.py track_classifications, add armed_sticky flag
      → Clear only if: unarmed_confidence > 0.85 for 3+ consecutive frames
      → Safety-critical: false negative on armed more dangerous than false positive


## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## PHASE 3: ENROLLMENT QUALITY (Medium Priority)
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## Prevents garbage-in-garbage-out at enrollment time.

- [ ] Redundancy filter: Reject embeddings with >0.92 cosine similarity to existing
      → In enroll.py process_enrollment(), check new embedding vs existing centroid
      → Skip if too similar - diminishing returns, wastes index space
      → Log: "Skipping redundant embedding for {person_id}"

- [ ] Outlier filter: Reject embeddings with <0.55 similarity to running centroid
      → Computed after 3+ embeddings exist for identity
      → Catches mislabeled photos, severe quality issues
      → Log warning: "Outlier embedding rejected for {person_id}: {similarity:.3f}"

- [ ] Per-identity quality report: Generate enrollment summary with metrics
      → Output: pose_variance, quality_mean, quality_std, embedding_count
      → Flag identities with low diversity or high variance as "weak enrollment"


## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## PHASE 4: PERFORMANCE OPTIMIZATION (Medium Priority)
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## Platform-agnostic speed improvements.

- [ ] Batched embedding extraction: Accumulate 2-4 faces before calling embedder
      → In run_runtime.py process_frame(), collect face_rois list
      → Call face_embedder.extract_batch(rois) if len >= 2
      → Amortizes ONNX session overhead, ~20-30% faster for multi-face frames

- [ ] Skip embedding for CONFIRMED tracks: Only track, don't re-embed
      → Already have skip_recognition flag, ensure it's respected in hot loop
      → Reduce embedding calls by 50%+ in steady-state with confirmed identities

- [ ] Adaptive sample interval: Increase embedding_sample_interval for stable tracks
      → SUSPECT: sample every 3 frames (need quick decision)
      → FRIENDLY: sample every 5 frames (building confidence)
      → CONFIRMED: sample every 30 frames (re-verification only)

- [ ] INT8 quantization: Create quantized model variants
      → Use onnxruntime.quantization or ONNX-TensorRT for INT8 models
      → Expected 2-3x speedup on supported hardware (Jetson, Intel)
      → Create tools/quantize_models.py script


## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## PHASE 5: TEMPORAL ACCUMULATION (Low Priority - Nice to Have)
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

- [ ] Body classification averaging: Smooth CLIP classification over time
      → Maintain EMA of classification scores per track
      → classification_ema = 0.7 * old + 0.3 * new
      → Reduces flickering between soldier/civilian/armed labels

- [ ] Graceful degradation flags: Maintain state but indicate uncertainty
      → Add uncertainty_level field to TrackStateMachine (0.0 - 1.0)
      → Increase when: quality drops, occlusion detected, score drops
      → Display as: "FRIENDLY (uncertain)" in UI overlay


